==English==

===Etymology===
First attested in 1615.    From Old French '''[[sompnolent]]''' ( > French '''[[#French|somnolent]]'''), < {{etyl|la}} '''[[somnolentus#Latin|somnolentus]]''' < '''[[somnus#Latin|somnus]]''' "sleep".  Replaced older form: [[sompnolent]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈsɒmnələnt/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈsɑːmnələnt/}}
* {{audio|en-us-somnolent.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[drowsy|Drowsy]] or [[sleepy]].
# {{dated}} Causing literal or figurative  sleepiness; [[soporific]].

